I don't know Koa really well, but somewhere a function call must be done to send the data back to you clients, as far as I know they use a lot `async/await`, probably they are doing something there.
But again, I'm not a koa user.

Regarding the `.send` api is needed, because we perform different operation once you call it, such as hooks and logging.

If you want you can also use `async/await` and just return the value:
```js
fastify.get('/return', async (req, reply) => {
  return { hello: 'world' }
})
```

Check out the docs about [reply](https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/master/docs/Reply.md#promises) :)
